<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03RM">Definition <span data-tag="03RM">4.9.3.10</span> <span class="named">(Regular Cardinals)</span>.</a> Let $\kappa $ be a cardinal. We say that $\kappa $ is <em>regular</em> if it is infinite and $\mathrm{cf}(\kappa ) = \kappa $. Here $\mathrm{cf}(\kappa )$ denotes the cofinality of $\kappa $ (Definition <a data-tag="03QN" href="/tag/03QN">4.9.1.28</a>). We say that $\kappa $ is <em>singular</em> if it is infinite but not regular. </p>
